{"title":"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, the volume of the rectangular prism is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b919d72838355d0d5fbe6e6d9bf0825836b4d525.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 72 \\text{ cm}^{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 48 \\text{ cm}^{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 64 \\text{ cm}^{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 24 \\text{ cm}^{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 14 \\text{ cm}^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"567\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the fact that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Volume\" title=\"Volume\">volume</a> of a rectangular prism is the length multiplied by the width multiplied by the height. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the volume of the prism. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/b/50b9a6f8d398257b274247e94a49c8899e73b99a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = 4 \\times 2 \\times 8 = 8 \\times 8 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 64 \\text{ cm}^{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"300\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.